SUMMARY:Monte Rio Redwoods 
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nThis is one of My Favorite local places to hik
 e. There are spectacular views of the Willow Creek watershed and miles of 
 hiking trails thru redwood forests dappled with sunlight.\n**This Trailhea
 d Has Very Limited Parking.**\n**You Must Have Zero No Shows to Attend.**\
 n**Everyone will start on the Waitlist.**\n**Please Do Not just show up fo
 r this hike!!!**\n\n**Where We Meet/Important Directions**\nDue to limited
  parking and the desire to accommodate as many hikers as possible everyone
  must carpool!\n**Meet and be ready to leave by \\*830am\\* from the commu
 ter parking lot at the corner of Graton Rd. & Main St. in Occidental.**\nG
 ive yourself plenty of time to arrive\, it often takes longer than you thi
 nk. Especially this one!\n\n**The Hike**\nFern Springs\, Eastside\, Deadwo
 od\, Koerber\, Upper Freeze Out\, Blair Witch\, West Panties and East Pant
 ies trails - A loop hike\nLength - +/-5.25 miles/8.45 kilometers\nElevatio
 n change - +/-985 feet/252 meters\nDifficulty - 7+/10 moderately strenuous
 \nExposures - 40% sun /60% shade - rocky\, poison oak\, ticks and insects.
 \nBring plenty of water. At least 68 oz. /2 liters.\nDogs - No\, only beca
 use we're car pooling.\nFacilities at trail head - None! Plan ahead.\nCost
  - $5 cash\nParking - **Meet and be ready to leave by 830am from the commu
 ter parking lot at the corner of Graton Rd. & Main St. in Occidental.**\nR
 emember to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water\, snack/l
 unch\, layered clothing & trekking poles.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scented p
 roducts the day of a group hike!\nOf course\, we will all look out for eac
 h other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for their own safety and w
 ell-being during hikes.\n\n**After Hike Gathering**\nWild Flour Bakery\n14
 0 Bohemian Hwy\, Freestone\, CA 95472\n(707) 874-2938\n[https://wildflourb
 read.com/](https://wildflourbread.com/)\n\n**When We Meet**\nSunday May 3\
 , 2026\n8:30 am - 12:00 pm\nIf your plans change after you sign up even if
  you're on the waitlist\, please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you a
 re sick\, running a fever\, were exposed to or have tested positive for Co
 vid-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may be changed\, rescheduled or cance
 lled in case of excessive heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apoca
 lypse etc... Check your email the night before for any possible changes.
